inducing a fault at almost any vulnerable point within the
helper logic successfully degrades the system’s ability to
trigger the emergency landing. Furthermore, as detailed in the
hardware experiment results (Figure 19), the most prominent
fault-induced outcome was None. Forcing the flight controller
into a state of total inaction during an emergency battery level
proved to be the most reliable and devastating exploit in this
scenario
